    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "body": "### Description\n\nThere are currently 2 configs in the project, the linter and formatter, `ruff` and the LSP designed around it, `ruff-lsp` but ever since v0.5.1, `ruff` has included the lsp implementation, which can be accessed via `ruff server`.\n\nRecently, the `ruff-lsp` project was archived on GitHub, noting that it is deprecated along with a migration guide to `ruff`. The `ruff` config does mention that it is the new implementation but there is no indication in the `ruff-lsp` config that it should not be used.\n\nIn this situation, I only see 2 options:\n1. Either `ruff-lsp` should be removed, or\n2. There should be a warning in the `ruff-lsp` config documentation that it is deprecated and that it is suggested to migrate to `ruff`",
    "closed_at": "2026-07-01T17:07:02Z",
