        {
            "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
            "body": "Hi I'm very new to how the project works internally, the CONTRIBUTING.md suggests that when deprecating a config, the contents should be changed like this:\n\n```lua\n---@type vim.lsp.Config\nreturn vim.tbl_extend('force', vim.lsp.config.systemd_lsp, {\n  on_init = function(...)\n    vim.deprecate('systemd_ls', 'systemd_lsp', '3.0.0', 'nvim-lspconfig', false)\n    if vim.lsp.config.systemd_lsp.on_init then\n      vim.lsp.config.systemd_lsp.on_init(...)\n    end\n  end,\n})\n```\n\nDoes it mean that the previous config should be shifted to `...` inside `vim.lsp.config.ruff_lsp.on_init()`? Like this:\n\n```lua\n---@type vim.lsp.Config\nreturn vim.tbl_extend('force', vim.lsp.config.ruff_lsp, {\n  on_init = function()\n    vim.deprecate('ruff_lsp', 'ruff', '0.0.62', 'nvim-lspconfig', false)\n    if vim.lsp.config.ruff_lsp.on_init then\n      vim.lsp.config.ruff_lsp.on_init({\n        cmd = { 'ruff-lsp' },\n        filetypes = { 'python' },\n        root_markers = { 'pyproject.toml', 'ruff.toml', '.git' },\n        ---@type lspconfig.settings.ruff_lsp\n        settings = {},\n      })\n    end\n  end,\n})\n```\n\nIs this correct? or does the function for `on_init` have to take in some arguments which also need to be passed on to `vim.lsp.config.ruff_lsp.on_init()`? Also what version should be passed into `vim.deprecate`? I set it to the last release version of ruff-lsp before it was archived, is that correct?",
