            "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
            "body": "Okay so I checked [`lsp/volar.lua`](https://github.com/neovim/nvim-lspconfig/blob/master/lsp/volar.lua) and [`lsp/vscoqtop.lua`](https://github.com/neovim/nvim-lspconfig/blob/master/lsp/vscoqtop.lua), and both of them seem to use the new lsp config inside `vim.tlb_extend`. But then yeah I do not understand why they're extending the newer config to show the warning for the older config, it makes no sense. Also both of them have completely removed the previous config, so it appears you would not be able to use the old config anyways.\n\nIs there some internal script that redirects `vim.lsp.enable(<old_config>)` to 'vim.lsp.enable(<new_config>)` automatically?",
